WEBVTT

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.190
I'm back!

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.550
That's weird.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.400
It's supposed to be here...

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.790
What's the manner, Touma? Is something wrong?

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.680
Yeah... Did you see my pudding, Natsuki?

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.980
I thought I put it in here...

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.430
Please let me stay overnight.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.940
What...?

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.150
What happened?

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.220
This is sudden.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:11.100
Sudden?

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.320
What's sudden is that you came over this evening without even contacting us first.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.640
What is it this time? Did you fight with your brother again?

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:25.970
Spot on, wasn't I?

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.390
Okay! Let me guess the reason for your quarrel...

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:35.420
Your brother ate your long awaited pudding bought from <i>that</i> corner store in front of the station or...

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.880
...something, huh?

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.360
I won't ask about your situation.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.030
Yeah... We shouldn't pry.

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:52.640
Every household has its own problems.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:57.800
Anyway, we should contact your family.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.360
Indeed.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.600
You didn't say anything and just came over after all...

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.940
Even though it has nothing to do with us...

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:07.600
Grudges held due to food sure are scary...

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.730
Yeah, scary...

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:12.810
Natsuki-kun?

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.290
Touma-san is at my place right now...

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:17.040
...but the situation is kind of weird.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:18.840
Yeah...

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:20.520
Huh?

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.950
It was <i>you</i> who ate the pudding from <i>that</i> shop?

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.290
...especially sweet foods, right?

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.080
Although it has nothing to do with us...

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.520
Get this through your thick skull, okay?

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.140
<i>That</i> store in front of the station, you see...

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.000
Even if it's just one pudding...

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.440
The ones from <i>that</i> store in front of the station are really good!

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.890
Yep! Yep

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:43.140
<i>That</i> shop is really something.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.440
Please do not belittle sweets!

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.020
Eating sweets?

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.770
Geez, he's too naive!

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:52.930
Was it sweet?

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.710
Naive!

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:57.210
Touma can stay over at our place for the time being.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.440
Sorry about this...

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.590
It's all right, isn't it ?

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:01.860
Shall we have some tea?

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.150
Thanks!

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:04.880
Please wait a while...

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.510
Speaking of the pudding from <i>that</i> store in front of the station...

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:16.250
We bought three of them today.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.010
That's right...

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.430
What's the matter, Haruka?

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.600
There are only two puddings left...

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.200
Seems like someone's at the door...

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:06.300
Hello everyone.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.100
Oh, it's just Takeru.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.110
Yes, it's me... Uncle Takeru.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:13.540
Sorry, but it's not time for your debut.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:17.960
I must show my face occasionally or you might just forget me.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.470
Like you would for relatives...

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:21.200
Here's is a present.

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:24.990
Puddings from the shop in front of the station.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.660
What?!

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:31.940
What?

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:34.850
Erm...

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:40.710
Actually, I ate a third of my share.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:44.680
That was what I thought and ate another third.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:51.680
After I saw Kana do that, I thought it was Kana's so I finished the remaining third.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.860
I knew it was Kana's fault!

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:59.270
But, I left some!

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:02.030
It's because Kana did such ambiguous things!

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:04.810
How many did you buy, anyway?

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:07.600
What happened here, exactly?

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:15.880
Here, Uncle.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.130
I'm fine, you girls can have it.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.540
It's like Haruka said... Please have one.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.450
Really?

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.300
Thanks.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:27.900
Here.

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:29.290
But...

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:31.010
Quit being so polite and just take it.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.170
Please go ahead.

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.240
Enjoy it.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.020
Thanks.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.840
Kana-chan will definitely like it.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:41.270
Here.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:44.260
My family out in the country sent me all this fruit.

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:45.420
Please take this.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.240
What's the matter with the both of you?

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:58.640
Hey Kana... What does she mean by "take"?

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.520
It could mean that she is giving it to us.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:02.420
I see...

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:04.280
Thanks.

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:13.840
This... That's right... I'll go peel it.

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:16.640
It's fine to just eat it like that.

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:21.550
Uchida?

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:25.710
For someone who's seen as many apples as Haruka,

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.830
She knows just what it wants to be.

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:31.450
Is that so?

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:35.510
Haruka's acting weird.

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:44.040
Oh, it's you Uchida... You came back.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:45.410
Yep, I've just arrived.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:48.250
Chiaki... Uchida brought apples.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:52.290
Wha-? I see...

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:53.920
Thanks...

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:57.740
Sorry Uchida, please play with Kana instead.

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.390
I'm not feeling well.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:02.930
Wait! Chiaki... Chiaki!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:11.050
Chiaki's acting weird, too.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:14.080
You came at the right time, Uchida.

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:19.700
You came at the right time, really.

00:09:20.610 --> 00:09:22.720
Kana-chan seems to be fine...

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.850
Oh, right... Uchida,

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:27.810
You must be tired after traveling so much.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.590
Those times when you get tired,

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:32.280
it's best to eat sweet foods, right?

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:48.920
Well then...

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:51.230
Kana-chan?

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.690
I'm going to the toilet.

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:02.560
You must never look at the contents of that cardboard box.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.710
K-Kana-chan...

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:50.540
Dear me... How can this...

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:53.020
You saw it.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.090
Oh... Ka-Kana-chan!

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:00.830
I told you not to look at it.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.850
Kana-chan...

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:05.930
This is...

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:08.920
Everyone joyfully gave these to us.

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:11.750
Likewise, we received them with joy...

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:15.550
I'm sorry, I didn't know...

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.300
You don't have to apologize.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.380
It was given out of the kindness of your heart.

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.470
Thanks.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:27.000
Kana-chan...

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.040
But...

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.740
You saw it...

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:33.460
You better be ready to face the consequences.

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:35.730
Eh?

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:38.840
Hi!

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:40.250
Is Chiaki around?

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:41.980
Hello, Kana.

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:45.220
Hey Touma, I'm glad you came empty-handed.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:47.460
I can't come without bringing anything?

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.980
Oh... Uchida came by, too.

00:11:56.550 --> 00:11:59.300
I came over because I wanted to eat some snacks. Darn...

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:00.440
Is there any left?

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:03.840
Haruka is making lots of fried apples if you want some.

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:07.740
Fried apples?! That's great! I can down at least five or six of them.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.620
I see... Five or six, you say?

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:12.390
Uchida had only two and she's out.

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:20.630
I'm back...

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:23.510
Welcome back, Touma.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:26.780
What's wrong with you, Touma? You don't seem well.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:35.700
Here, a present from Haruka.

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:42.490
Hey...

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.780
What's the meaning of this apple?

00:13:14.590 --> 00:13:15.850
Is it Touma?

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:17.640
Touma?

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:18.990
What about her?

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:24.080
Nothing... I was just mumbling.

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:33.490
Oh... Yes.

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:37.460
Let's make this apple into something that Touma would like.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:39.920
Oh... What would that be?

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:50.760
Fried Apples.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.880
Oh...

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:08.860
...so do you know what you did wrong that caused you to fail?

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.030
Hmmm... I see.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:14.910
Eh? You're doing it now?

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:17.420
Okay, try it then.

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:20.750
Hmmm... Yep.

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:23.950
Who is Haruka talking to?

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:26.590
My brother, Natsuki.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.510
Haven't you met him before?

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:31.180
You mean that big fellow?

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.270
Oh, there's someone like that.

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:34.850
So, what are they talking about?

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:40.610
Natsuki is better at cooking, but he's poor at making sweet stuff.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:46.290
That's why I told him to ask Great Teacher Haruka.

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:50.010
I see... so Great Teacher Haruka is teaching him now, huh?

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:52.090
Didn't I say that was wrong?!

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:53.310
Great Teacher!

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:55.410
Hey, Chiaki.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:15:00.240
Has Haruka ever been so emotionally charged with anyone before?

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:05.550
Will she fall in love with him?

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:14.120
Hmph. Impossible.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:21.900
That guy is not in the "People whom Haruka-neesama can be entrusted to" folder in my heart.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:24.900
Do you have the right to pick her boyfriend?

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.980
And, what's with that folder?

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.960
It's definitely empty.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:34.600
Their relationship will reach the point where they'll teach each other to cook sweet and spicy food one day.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:35.870
Shut up!

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:40.470
If it comes to that, you will cook!

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:46.170
Now go and help finish the curry that Haruka-neesama is making.

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:48.990
Take it as your cooking training.

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:51.210
But... But...

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:52.030
Hey...

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:59.740
It's been really great for me to have been able to meet Chiaki, Kana, and Haruka.

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:03.980
T-Touma...

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:06.410
Is the curry done?

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:08.360
The reason must be because there's food to eat.

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:11.760
Okay... That phone call will be pretty long.

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:13.340
We will finish it.

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:15.830
Okay, let's do it seriously.

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:18.350
Oh, by the way, what do you want for toppings?

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:20.460
We can decide that later.

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:21.120
Eggs.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:22.870
Okay, eggs it is.

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:25.030
Hey, Chiaki, pass the eggs.

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:26.880
Didn't I say it now's not the time.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.610
Sunny side up would be nice.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:31.620
Yeah... The egg should be sunny side up.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:34.550
Now, after breaking the eggs add the yolk in,

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:35.800
then add some sugar.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:37.310
Okay, I got it.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:43.190
Hey, why are you adding sugar?

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:45.490
Didn't someone tell me to add sugar?

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:46.970
I didn't say anything.

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:50.370
Not sugar, but curry powder. Curry powder!

00:16:50.370 --> 00:16:52.740
Yes, then add the curry powder.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:53.890
Yes.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:56.820
Did you sift it?

00:16:57.470 --> 00:16:58.910
Put it in a dish...

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:01.120
...then put it in the preheated oven.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:02.270
Put it in the oven.

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:04.030
Huh? Put it in the oven?!

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:13.340
Isn't it a little too sweet?

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:16.450
Even if you say so, I did it according to the instructions.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:18.140
Hmmm... add some salt then.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:21.570
Pass the salt, Touma.

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:26.040
What the hell are you doing now?!

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:29.120
You're completely useless!

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:32.400
I'm back...

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:35.360
I'm hungry.

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:38.750
Eh? Did you not eat at their place?

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:41.970
What was cooked was inedible.

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:45.620
Hey, Touma.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:49.020
You're hungry, right? Want to try this?

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:52.600
What's that?

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.750
It smells like curry...

00:17:56.750 --> 00:17:58.970
Oh, it's true, after all...

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:37.230
You ate my pudding again, didn't you?!

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:47.990
Do you have any proof that it was yours?

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.000
I wrote my name on the cover...

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.000
Look!

00:19:57.260 --> 00:20:01.910
I thought that was merely some design and I didn't pay attention to it!

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:03.470
What the?!

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:06.600
Hey Natsuki, you're at fault here.

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:08.430
Apologize to Touma.

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:12.020
Hey Natsuki! Are you listening?

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:12.920
Hey.

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:22.830
This is your fault.

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.480
You should apologize to Touma.

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:31.850
I'll buy another one for you since it's my fault.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:36.290
I'll never forgive you!

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:43.970
...and that's what happened, so please let me stay over for the night.

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:45.970
Again...

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:51.400
We don't have any more pudding; how about omelet rice instead?

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:52.560
Thank you...

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:56.330
I'll talk to Natsuki about this.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.640
Thank you...

00:20:58.310 --> 00:21:00.410
It's fine, this is what should be done.

00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:04.250
Okay, I'll start preparing dinner.

00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:05.610
Thank you.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:18.340
But... Your brother might have some valid reason...

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:21.500
What?! Why are you siding with him?!

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:22.840
No, I'm not.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:25.890
If you scribble your name so small that others can't see it, it's useless.

00:21:27.420 --> 00:21:29.350
If you want to write, write it BIG!

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:31.620
Okay? Look carefully...

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:38.360
Just like this.

00:21:44.770 --> 00:21:45.860
Say, Kana...

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:46.950
What's with this 100?

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:50.090
From the number 10, add a circle...

00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:51.260
...and it becomes Touma.

00:21:51.260 --> 00:21:53.630
What? You're a genius!

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:56.640
Okay, I'll try it too.

00:21:57.710 --> 00:21:59.270
How's this?

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:13.110
"Plus" can be pronounced as <i>kuwaeru</i>, right?

00:22:15.330 --> 00:22:18.010
Add the number 7 behind it...

00:22:18.010 --> 00:22:20.400
...shorten it, and it becomes Kana.

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:24.050
What? You're a genius too!

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:29.050
How will this work out in practice?

00:22:29.050 --> 00:22:31.530
Will others understand it?

00:22:32.350 --> 00:22:33.930
Oh yeah...

00:22:33.930 --> 00:22:35.640
It might be too subtle.

00:22:35.640 --> 00:22:37.670
Chiaki, what do you think of this?

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:42.190
I heard the explanation from you guys so...

00:22:42.190 --> 00:22:44.970
...why not ask Haruka-neesama?

00:22:44.970 --> 00:22:45.920
That's true.

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:48.550
I'm not sure though...

00:22:48.550 --> 00:22:51.850
If Haruka-neesama sees it, then I'll agree.

00:22:51.850 --> 00:22:55.140
I don't know... But you seem confident.

00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:58.120
Okay, eat up everyone.

00:22:58.840 --> 00:22:59.660
Haruka!

00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:00.610
Yes?

00:23:00.610 --> 00:23:02.200
What do you think of this?

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:18.250
107?

00:23:19.320 --> 00:23:21.330
She combined it.

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:24.550
I'm right, aren't I? 107...

00:23:24.550 --> 00:23:26.050
Yes, it's 107.

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:29.060
She combined it.

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:32.970
Takeru does some good deeds once in a while.

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:34.960
I'm glad if everyone is happy.

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:36.470
You actually knew <i>that</i> shop.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:38.810
That's Reiko-san's favourite shop.

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:39.480
Ah!

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:41.970
Next time on Minami-ke Okaeri.

00:23:41.970 --> 00:23:43.190
There should be an order.

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:44.360
Reiko-san!
